{"type": "message", "id": "38eab1bd", "parentId": "453bceb2", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T18:24:04.336Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_df8b60160e53408f94d77fe8", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"SEER cancer survival rates 5-year lung liver esophageal brain ovarian\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 888,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4a40b311d891faa5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSEER Cancer Stat Facts\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4a40b311d891faa5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0d3d77c38fc29fd3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThese summaries provide statistics for common cancer types. The statistics include incidence, mortality, survival, stage, prevalence, and lifetime risk. Links to additional resources are included. Updated annually.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0d3d77c38fc29fd3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"022d0052854d6628\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer survival and incidence from the Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results (SEER) program - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"022d0052854d6628\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14657533/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a4ffd9000f76932d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChanges during the time period 1992-2000 are summarized by the annual percent change in SEER incidence and U.S. mortality data for this period. Five-year relative survival for selected cancers is examined by stage at diagnosis, based on data from 1990-1999. In addition, 5-year conditional survival for patients already surviving for 1-3 years after diagnosis is discussed as well as relative survival for other time periods.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a4ffd9000f76932d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1579a71c5e973112\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSEER*Explorer - National Cancer Institute\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1579a71c5e973112\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statistics-network/explorer/overview.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"119a9f1a7d87c73c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSEER*Explorer provides access to cancer statistics (rates and trends) for a cancer site by sex, race, calendar year, stage, and histology. Users can create custom graphs and tables, download data and images, download SEER*Stat sessions, and share results.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"119a9f1a7d87c73c\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ddf193b76de72b7a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer statistics, 2024 - Siegel - 2024 - CA: A Cancer Journal for Clinicians - Wiley Online Library\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ddf193b76de72b7a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://acsjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.3322/caac.21820\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6b43899a57a35ea8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe 5-year relative survival rate for all cancers combined has increased from 49% for diagnoses during the mid-1970s to <strong>69% during 2013–2019</strong> (Table 6).4, 5 Current survival is highest for cancers of the thyroid (99%), prostate (97%), testis ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6b43899a57a35ea8\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 17, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"acsjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"734727f173ae5856\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSurveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results Program\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"734727f173ae5856\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a7b90467bc4f8a19\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAn authoritative source for cancer statistics in the US. We collect incidence, prevalence and survival data and publish reports on these and cancer mortality. For those interested in cancer statistics and surveillance methods.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a7b90467bc4f8a19\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "SEER cancer survival rates 5-year lung liver esophageal brain ovarian", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 888, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4a40b311d891faa5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSEER Cancer Stat Facts\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4a40b311d891faa5\">>>", "url": "https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0d3d77c38fc29fd3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThese summaries provide statistics for common cancer types. The statistics include incidence, mortality, survival, stage, prevalence, and lifetime risk. Links to additional resources are included. Updated annually.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0d3d77c38fc29fd3\">>>", "siteName": "seer.cancer.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"022d0052854d6628\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer survival and incidence from the Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results (SEER) program - PubMed\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"022d0052854d6628\">>>