{"type": "message", "id": "fb90fa63", "parentId": "ebcce33f", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T18:24:13.497Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_da736383e662410da2c2785d", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"\\\"chordoma\\\" annual cases United States incidence number\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 3,\n  \"tookMs\": 1003,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dc85b374bbb0a38e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma: Practice Essentials, History of the Disease, Epidemiology\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dc85b374bbb0a38e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/250902-overview\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5dbab217fb003108\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma is a rare tumor that occurs along the axial spine in children and in adults, with an incidence of approximately <strong>350 cases per year</strong> in the United States [6] and a reported annual worldwide incidence of 0.08 per 100,000 cases.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5dbab217fb003108\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"emedicine.medscape.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"729e1d7a64600977\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDescriptive epidemiology of chordomas in the United States - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"729e1d7a64600977\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32342333/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"eb42e314f5e2cce1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe most common location was cranial (38.7%), followed by sacral (34.3%) and spinal (27.0%). The average age-adjusted incidence rate was <strong>0.088 per 100,000 persons per year</strong> (95% CI 0.086-0.091), with an annual percentage change of 1.29% (95% ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"eb42e314f5e2cce1\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7d852a2b3fe545ac\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma: incidence and survival patterns in the United States, 1973-1995 - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7d852a2b3fe545ac\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11227920/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"36eb438ed9fcbf6a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nResults: The age-adjusted chordoma incidence rate (IR) of <strong>0.08 per 100,000</strong> was age-dependent, more common in males (IR 0.10) than females (IR 0.06) and rare among patients aged &lt;40 years and blacks.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"36eb438ed9fcbf6a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "\"chordoma\" annual cases United States incidence number", "provider": "brave", "count": 3, "tookMs": 1003, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dc85b374bbb0a38e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChordoma: Practice Essentials, History of the Disease, Epidemiology\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dc85b374bbb0a38e\">>>", "url": "https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/250902-overview", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5dbab217fb003108\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChordoma is a rare tumor that occurs along the axial spine in children and in adults, with an incidence of approximately <strong>350 cases per year</strong> in the United States [6] and a reported annual worldwide incidence of 0.08 per 100,000 cases.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5dbab217fb003108\">>>", "siteName": "emedi